xmonad-log-applet (3.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream version 3.0.0.
  * The settings schema is renamed to org.xmonad.log-applet. Saved
    settings are kept.
  * Install NEWS.md with the other documentation in
    xmonad-log-applet-common.
  * Add debian/copyright.

 -- Karl Ljungkvist <dev@kalj.se>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:38:08 +0000

xmonad-log-applet (2.90.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build the applet for all three supported panels, as separate packages:
    xmonad-log-applet-mate, xmonad-log-applet-xfce (Xfce panel 4.14 or
    later) and xmonad-log-applet-gnome (gnome-panel 3.38 or later).
  * Move the settings schema and icon, which all three use, to the new
    xmonad-log-applet-common, along with the README and the example
    xmonad.hs.
  * The MATE applet was in the package xmonad-log-applet, which
    xmonad-log-applet-mate and xmonad-log-applet-common replace.
  * Add libxfce4panel-2.0-dev and libgnome-panel-dev to Build-Depends.

 -- Karl Ljungkvist <dev@kalj.se>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 09:18:06 +0000

xmonad-log-applet (2.90.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream version 2.90.0, a preview of 3.0. Only the MATE panel is
    supported for now.
  * Icons: only a left click activates a window, so a right click reaches
    the panel menu. Windows without an icon get a generic one instead of
    being left out.
  * A failed X connection no longer crashes the applet, and all applets in
    a process share one X connection.
  * A malformed workspace in a message from xmonad is skipped and logged,
    instead of blanking the applet.
  * Use GDBus instead of the deprecated dbus-glib. The subscription is
    removed when the applet is destroyed.
  * Drop libdbus-glib-1-dev and intltool from Build-Depends.
  * Run the new unit tests for the message parser during the build.
  * Sample xmonad.hs: based on mateConfig, marks urgent workspaces and
    formats its messages with dynamicLogWithPP. It needs xmonad-contrib
    0.17 or later.

 -- Karl Ljungkvist <dev@kalj.se>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:20:10 +0100

